<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14252" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">discussor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an examiner</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip.
				1, 21, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., in the later period of the empire, <i>one who revised the accounts of the public
			revenue</i> in the provinces, <i>an auditor</i>, Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογοθέτης</span>, <i><span class="en">Cod.
					Just. 10</span></i>, tit. 30; <i><span class="en">Symm.
				Ep. 5, 76 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
